mantle rm245
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_frida_rainhand
title the folded hill
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=none quarter=sump
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk folds_hills_into_scraps_of_map
likes honey_cakes old_tales old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes cold_tea deep_mud
fears losing_the_view_in_a_fold
hopes a_window_level_with_the_heights
topics land +0.6 dreams +0.5 memories +0.3 gossip -0.6
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=indirect tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# creases scraps of old maps into hills and keeps the summit window folded out of sight.

words
oath! = Flatten my hill | Frost my sill over
saying! = A fold can hide an entire hill | Climb twice before drawing once
hillpaper = a paper ridge | a creased hill
blankgap = the empty square | a gap between the streets
glaze = a sticky golden skin | a thin honey crust
wrongturn = the road drawn crooked | a bend drawn backward
workcloth = my square of wiping cloth | a rag from my pocket
spice = a burnt honey edge | a sticky corner
foldmark = a worn white crease | a fold going pale
toproom = a room looking out | a high room
rimestripe = a white frost line | a rime of white
hulls = the sweep of a stern | the rake of a mast
ruler = a straight sliver of wood | a straight bit of lath
steeppath = the hard climb | a long rise
sill = the dry interior ledge | a narrow ledge

any
opinion houses against 3 : A House gets its whole roof on a map. Down here my entire street fits under a dot.
opinion city for 2 : I mean to see every roof in town from above. That ambition's one thing I owe this place.
opinion dole for 2 : A full belly gives me the leisure to want something beyond tomorrow's meal.
opinion strangers against 1 : I'll show the public turning to anybody. The walk to my own door I keep folded up.
opinion merchants against 2 : Little cakes shrink in the same old wrapper until the paper seems the better bargain.
opinion sump for 1 : I learned every way up by starting down here. I still know the way back.

grown
line greet : Step round the fold. There's room. Welcome. | Just enough space for us both to stand easily.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : I can give a stranger a little width of pavement. | Come as far as my shadow.
line greet.return : Welcome in your turn. I've put the paper away. | Good to have you level with me.
line again.open : Same stretch of road again. | Our paths cross pretty neatly.
line farewell : Find the turning you set out for. | Take the ascent at your own pace.
line farewell.return : And may your way show up plain. | Your kind words will travel in a dry fold.
line react.news : Let me hear which direction the news came from. | My eyes will follow your account to its edge.
line react.news.new : That puts another street on my paper. | My old map hasn't a mark for that.
line react.news.known : I've travelled the edge of that account before. | That one's on my sheet already.
line react.news.doubt : There's an odd corner where those claims ought to join. | I'd leave that stretch in pencil.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : I'd climb a bit for news like that. | That's worth a light in the upper window.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|assault] : Some hurts look larger the closer you come. | Leave the talk there. There's grief enough.
line answer.how : Keeping my higher hopes under cover. | I'm moving, even when the street looks level.
line ask.how : How far did your plans carry you? | Was today much of an uphill walk?
line sympathise : There's a place to sit without being seen. | Step into my shelter a moment.
line ack : I can see where your line's going. | That much is clear from here.
line refuse : I've a thing half done that takes both paws. | Another time, when I've seen to my own errands.
line accept_decline : I'll fold that away for another occasion. | You've your own road to walk.
line preclose : I ought to take the rest of my climb in daylight. | There's a turning I've yet to reach today.
line accept_preclose : Go before the way gets crowded underfoot. | Best leave while you can choose your own pace.

scene map
when topic=land self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Old ink sends a road straight through a hill. | My map's wrong at a place I love.
b : Would you scratch it out? | Will you get a new one?
a : I'd fold the sheet at the hill. Let the road climb visibly. | I like knowing one thing the maker never learned.


scene heights
when topic=dreams here.region=ridgemere
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like the sort of window where rain arrives sideways. | I'd pay dearly for first light on my own floor.
b : Up in the Heights? | Does the sun cost more uphill?
a : High enough for a clear view, anyway. I'm keeping the sill bare. | The light's free. The boards under it are dear.


scene ship
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A ship's name comes to me from the shape under the sail. | I know the ships better from far off.
b : Without seeing the flag? | How do you see their names?
a : Paint can change overnight. A stern takes a little longer. | In their outlines. Up close one great wall of wood looks like another.


scene honey
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I break a honey cake where the top cracks first. | The sticky wrapper's worth taking away.
b : Is there an art to eating one? | For the crumbs?
a : Only the art of getting two crisp edges with one break. | And for the smell. My pocket gets to be a bakery for an hour.


scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Frost draws every sloping tile on the roofs. | You can see a path growing under the frost.
b : You could copy that into a map. | Before anybody walks it?
a : For half an hour. Then the warm chimneys rub it out. | Where the stones hold heat. The white goes thin first.


scene tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : My tea goes cold while I'm tracing roads. | There goes another day, cooling in my cup.
b : Why not drink before drawing? | Can it be warmed again?
a : I mean to every time. There's that one last turning. | I can at least set tomorrow's cup nearer the fire.


scene story
when topic=memories self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The old tales I remember have one thing the teller could touch. | I don't care whether a tale's castle stood on that very hill.
b : Such as a sword? | What do you care about?
a : An onion would do. I'm curious how that papery skin felt. | Whether you can hear the stairs protest under the feet coming down.


scene work
when topic=work self.job=none self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Coming away from #self.workplace#, I clean one paw before feeling for my map. | I notice which way my shadow falls on my walk from work.
b : Why only one? | Does it help you find home?
a : The cloth's small. My second paw must wait till I get home. | It tells me how much daylight I have for walking farther.


scene window
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A window wide enough to lean both elbows in would suit me. | I keep a paper window folded shut.
b : That's a little dream. | Can you see through it?
a : There's a whole hillside outside it. I've only priced the elbows. | I get to decide what's outside. For now, that's enough.


scene gull
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull can blot out a ship if it crosses close enough. | I drew a gull as large as the market on my first map.
b : Ever mistake one for a sail? | Was it a very grand bird?
a : Only until the sail folds both wings and lands. | It was standing on the sheet when I drew round its toes.


scene mud
when topic=weather self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mud takes the shape of a road I would never draw. | Cold mud finds the inside of my cuffs.
b : All swerves and potholes? | Why go out in it?
a : One long dead end waiting for my foot. | Hard to climb a hill from inside one's cupboard.


scene north
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know #self.street# by the way it catches its first light. | I've drawn home smaller than it lives in my head.
b : Even with the sun behind cloud? | Why leave so little room?
a : The roof edges turn pale in the same order. | The page wouldn't hold it otherwise.


scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd let #self.friend# look over my folded map. | I can listen to a familiar voice even while tracing a street.
b : A private map? | Does a stranger take more work?
a : The roads are public. The pencilled windows are mine. | I have to put the paper away to hear what's behind the words.


scene climb
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count a climb by the change in my breath. | I like taking two different streets up and down.
b : How far is one breath worth? | To give your feet some variety?
a : Depends what's waiting at the top. I get there faster for a view. | To give my paper another seam I know for myself.


scene times
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : These thin times keep pushing my window farther uphill. | Even the chalk for drawing a better room seems dear.
b : Are you giving up on it? | Can you still draw it?
a : I've only made the pencilled frame narrower. | I can fold the four walls out of scrap.


scene gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Some talk goes round three streets and comes back wearing a hat.
b : Are you willing to stand behind that? | Have you seen the hat before?
a : I'll stand behind hearing it. That's the limit. | Often enough to leave the latest tale where I found it.


scene hinge
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've drawn my upper room's door opening outward. | If my hill room had only one shelf I'd know what to put there.
b : Planning the way out already? | The old map?
a : I don't want a door eating the little floor I can afford. | A flat stone to keep the map from rolling.


scene ink
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : You can date a street on paper by the way the ink's worn. | A town drawn with brown ink looks warm even in frost.
b : Read a year from a smudge? | Which do you prefer looking at?
a : No. But somebody's thumb kept returning there. | Frost on the actual town. Brown ink in a pocket.


story room [topic=dreams]
  : I made a house of paper with a square window cut in the wall. I held it up on the climb.
  : At one bend it framed nothing but the Sound. At the next, a row of leaking gutters.
  b : Where did you set it down?
  : In my pocket. I wasn't buying the first view just because it was lovely.


story glaze [topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes]
  : A cake drew a perfect brown circle through my map where the paper folded round it.
  : I spent half the climb wondering what great wall I'd forgotten.
  b : When did you find out?
  : When I licked a sticky claw. I cut along the circle and now my town fits inside a cake.


story sailcloth [topic=travel]
  : I once named a distant ship for a pup who wouldn't take my word.
  : The little unbeliever wanted a second look. We waited till the wind blew hard.
  b : Was the name right?
  : It was a sheet hung between two poles. I thanked the pup, a bit stiffly. I look for the hull now.


rule @fold
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The pale cuts in the roofline show beautifully just now. | First light finds every fold I've missed.


rule @workrag
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=none
does aside
cooldown 8h
say My paper can wait till my paws are clean. | Set the scrap aside. There's still a clean corner on it.


rule @frost
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A cold morning makes straight edges easy to see. | White sky over that rise. Good walking light.


rule @road
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I'd like a line of sight over those roofs. | There's another climb to fit into the margin.

dlg resident.hub : The public roads are written out between my ears.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, there's one less unfamiliar turn in my day.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : There's no call to lean over my shoulder. My ears reach perfectly well.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dusk|night] : I can trace my way without the sheet at this hour.
dlg resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=none self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. It gets the daylight hours.
dlg resident.job : I like to come home with something to show for the climb.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This came into my hearing. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Somebody says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The blank edges are yours to judge.
dlg resident.bye : I hope the view's clear at your next turning.

graft resident.hub
choice Why keep a map that's wrong? -> wrong_map
node wrong_map
say Some roads disappear and leave their names behind. I like walking out with a sheet that knows both versions.
free
choice Which version would you give a traveller? -> wrong_map_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node wrong_map_more
say The one underfoot. I'd draw the old bend on a separate scrap for somebody curious.
choice I'll remember the bend. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
